{"uid":"cli/lazynmap_post.py","name":"lazynmap_post.py","qualname":"cli/lazynmap_post.py","kind":"module","file":"cli/lazynmap_post.py","line":1,"end_line":300,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Post-scan side effects executed at the tail of ``do_lazynmap``.","description":"Three artefacts are produced after every successful scan:\n\n1. ``sessions/recon_plan_<target>.md`` — operator + LLM-readable plan\n   generated by :func:`cli.recon_plan.build_recon_plan`.\n2. ``sessions/world_model.json`` — phase bumped to ``enum`` so the\n   daemon / autonomous loop / status bar agree we have just transitioned\n   past pure recon.\n3. ``sessions/autonomous_events.jsonl`` — one ``lazynmap.recon_plan``\n   event so MCP consumers (``lazyown_poll_events`` and the dashboard)\n   see the transition.\n\nEvery step is best-effort: failure in one branch must not block the\nothers or propagate back into :class:`LazyOwnShell`. The implementation\nis pure Python (no ``cmd2``, ``rich`` or ``flask`` imports) so the suite\ncan exercise it with hand-rolled fixtures.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["cli/lazynmap_post.py::PostScanConfig","cli/lazynmap_post.py::PostScanResult","cli/lazynmap_post.py::run_post_scan"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
